<title>USA: Mitsuzuka says yen not mentioned in G7 statement.</title>
<headline>Mitsuzuka says yen not mentioned in G7 statement.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka said that the communique from Sunday's G7 meeting does not make a specific reference to the recent moves of the Japanese yen.</p>
<p>Mitsuzuka made the remarks to Reuters as he came out of a meeting of finance officials from Group of Seven industrialized nations.</p>
<p>The communique is expected to be released shortly.</p>
</text>
